  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Buyers and factories pay for accuracy, on-time delivery and consistent quality. They judge you by specifications, inspections and follow-through.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing a clear specification sheet.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and textile and fashion technology: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools generate designs and summarise orders. Routine documentation shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Technical judgment, quality discipline and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to explore and check; later, own specifications and quality calls.
  </p>

